  "body": "## 更新内容（安卓 v0.1.30）\n\n这一版处理部分手机一键清理后，无障碍服务被系统停掉、开关却还显示开着的问题。\n\n- 有的手机用了一键清理或加速以后，系统会把涟漪的无障碍服务停掉，可设置里的开关还显示开着，这时涟漪拦不住 App。现在涟漪能认出这种情况，首页顶部会显示「涟漪没在拦截」。\n- 首页的提示卡、恢复拦截页和通知会告诉你怎么恢复：在系统的无障碍设置里先把涟漪关掉，再打开，点允许。点首页的提示卡会直接进系统的无障碍设置。\n- 通知在每次卡住时提醒一次，服务重新连上后自动收起。\n- 恢复拦截页在大字号下，步骤编号不再被裁掉。\n- 已知限制：识别和提示在测试里验证过，在 OPPO 手机上覆盖安装后服务正常连回，没有误报。卡住的状态还没在真机上复现过。这些改动只在安卓上有，iPhone 版没有更新，仍是 v0.1.5。\n\n## What's New (Android v0.1.30)\n\nThis release handles a problem on some phones where a one tap cleanup stops the accessibility service while the switch still shows on.\n\n- On some phones, after a one tap cleanup or speed boost, the system stops Ripple's accessibility service, but the switch in Settings still shows on, so Ripple cannot block apps. Ripple now detects this, and the top of the home screen says Ripple is not blocking.\n- The home screen card, the restore blocking page and a notification tell you how to fix it: in the system accessibility settings, turn Ripple off, turn it on again, and tap Allow. Tapping the card on the home screen opens the system accessibility settings.\n- The notification shows once each time the service gets stuck, and goes away when the service connects again.\n- With large text, the step numbers on the restore blocking page are no longer cut off.\n- Known limits: detection and the prompts were checked in tests, and on an OPPO phone the service reconnected after an update install with no false alert. The stuck state itself has not been reproduced on a real phone yet. These changes are Android only. The iPhone app was not updated and remains v0.1.5.\n",
